WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.900
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:34.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs & Migoto

01:35.370 --> 01:40.000
Episode 11:
The Secret of the Pendant

01:45.670 --> 01:46.600
Vitalis!

01:48.130 --> 01:48.780
Get out!

02:05.740 --> 02:07.040
Hey, Joli-Coeur!

02:07.040 --> 02:09.050
Joli-Coeur, wait!

02:11.690 --> 02:13.630
Remy, push faster!

02:13.630 --> 02:15.220
All right.

02:18.390 --> 02:19.810
Wait, wait!

02:24.040 --> 02:25.690
Hurry, hurry up!

02:25.690 --> 02:26.630
Made it!

02:27.780 --> 02:28.860
Okay!

02:29.570 --> 02:32.110
Got you.

02:42.450 --> 02:44.660
Your son is laughing happily.

02:44.660 --> 02:46.740
They must be having fun.

02:46.740 --> 02:49.010
He's become lively again.

02:49.010 --> 02:50.380
All thanks to Remy.

02:50.380 --> 02:53.890
Yes, they seem like a real brother and sister, laughing together.

02:54.880 --> 02:57.550
I wish this day would last forever.

02:59.410 --> 03:01.460
Joli-Coeur...

03:03.040 --> 03:04.650
Ah... Come here, Capi.

03:05.520 --> 03:06.150
Huh....?

03:14.710 --> 03:16.620
What's wrong, Joli-Coeur?

03:20.170 --> 03:21.850
Guys, what's wrong?

03:41.530 --> 03:42.850
Have you been all right, guys?

03:44.260 --> 03:45.710
Mr. Vitalis...

03:51.540 --> 03:53.130
Mr. Vitalis!

03:53.130 --> 03:54.110
Remy!

04:06.350 --> 04:07.880
Mr. Vitalis!

04:12.270 --> 04:13.400
Remy...

04:21.950 --> 04:25.730
Mr. Vitalis. I've been waiting, waiting for so long.

04:40.460 --> 04:42.120
The suspicion was cleared, right?

04:42.120 --> 04:45.690
No one will think you are the criminal, right?

04:45.690 --> 04:48.750
I heard the arsonist was caught in another town.

04:48.750 --> 04:52.680
He confessed to all the cases in the town of Toulouse.

04:52.680 --> 04:55.010
I'm happy for you that all the suspicions were cleared.

04:56.520 --> 04:58.290
Thank goodness!

04:59.590 --> 05:03.710
There are no words to show my gratitude.

05:03.710 --> 05:07.410
I was told by the police that Remy was here, and came to pick her up.

05:09.040 --> 05:11.770
Are you going to go traveling again?

05:13.580 --> 05:14.820
I am.

05:21.410 --> 05:22.580
Mr. Vitalis!

05:22.580 --> 05:24.980
I'm all right.

05:24.980 --> 05:26.490
I will feel better soon.

05:26.490 --> 05:29.760
You must be tired. Please take a rest.

05:29.760 --> 05:30.580
Oh no...

05:30.990 --> 05:33.290
No... Please do so.

05:33.290 --> 05:35.590
It's not good to overexert yourself.

05:36.190 --> 05:37.120
Here...

05:38.730 --> 05:41.210
If you need something, call me any time.

05:41.210 --> 05:42.600
Ah.... Thank you.

05:43.380 --> 05:45.380
Remy, I'm all right.

05:45.380 --> 05:46.280
But...

05:46.280 --> 05:49.980
I'm just a bit tired. I will feel better after a short nap.

05:50.760 --> 05:53.480
Now, you go and play with Arthur.

05:54.080 --> 05:54.950
Okay.

06:25.110 --> 06:25.640
Remy?

06:26.360 --> 06:26.970
Eh?

06:27.530 --> 06:29.720
Are you going with Mr. Vitalis?

06:29.720 --> 06:31.010
I am.

06:31.010 --> 06:33.470
It's because we're traveling artists.

06:33.470 --> 06:36.210
We go to different towns and perform our shows.

06:36.210 --> 06:37.230
I don't like it.

06:38.550 --> 06:39.740
Arthur...

06:39.740 --> 06:42.460
I don't want you to leave here.

06:42.460 --> 06:44.710
We've finally become friends.

06:51.420 --> 06:54.380
Arthur, I am sad, too.

06:54.380 --> 06:56.110
But I have to go.

06:56.110 --> 06:59.260
Remy, I want to show you my most precious treasure.

06:59.260 --> 07:00.480
Treasure?

07:00.480 --> 07:01.470
Yes.

07:03.550 --> 07:06.170
Wow... What a beautiful watch.

07:06.170 --> 07:07.830
It's my father's keepsake.

07:09.480 --> 07:12.430
Property of the Milligan family head.

07:12.430 --> 07:13.600
My mother said so.

07:20.850 --> 07:22.070
It seems almost alive.

07:22.610 --> 07:24.510
It's your most precious treasure, right?

07:25.700 --> 07:26.870
I'll give it to you.

07:26.870 --> 07:27.700
Eh?

07:27.700 --> 07:31.730
I'll give you my treasure. So please stay here. Please.

07:35.390 --> 07:36.670
No?

07:36.670 --> 07:37.940
Arthur.

07:41.850 --> 07:43.930
Oh... Yes.

07:43.930 --> 07:46.660
I want to show you my treasure.

07:46.660 --> 07:47.890
Remy's treasure?

07:47.890 --> 07:51.090
Yes. Look, this is my amulet.

07:53.310 --> 07:55.930
I've never shown it to anyone before.

07:55.930 --> 07:57.900
I'll only show it to you.

07:58.490 --> 07:59.900
I was a foundling.

07:59.900 --> 08:01.150
Huh...

08:01.470 --> 08:06.760
I was told I had this with me when I was found by Mr. Barberin in Chavanon village.

08:07.250 --> 08:10.410
Mother Barberin told me to keep this safe,

08:10.750 --> 08:15.460
because my real mother might have given this to me.

08:20.170 --> 08:21.050
Please.

08:21.060 --> 08:22.970
Thanks.

08:24.580 --> 08:27.800
Remy is a really cheerful and pretty girl, isn't she?

08:28.290 --> 08:31.560
Thanks to Remy, Arthur became lively, too.

08:35.130 --> 08:37.560
I had a baby girl, too.

08:39.160 --> 08:45.290
She was kidnapped by someone while my husband was sick.

08:46.010 --> 08:49.990
She would be Remy's age if she's alive.

08:51.890 --> 08:55.960
You are lucky for having such a pretty girl.

09:00.070 --> 09:03.710
Remy and I are not related by blood. She was a foundling.

09:04.120 --> 09:05.130
Huh?

09:06.080 --> 09:11.640
We have been traveling together since I rescued her from a slave trader.

09:13.310 --> 09:15.890
It doesn't seem like it happened.

09:19.370 --> 09:21.610
Remy's bright and cheerful attitude,

09:22.190 --> 09:25.440
brought us much happiness.

09:25.440 --> 09:29.030
I feel like we would be happier with Remy.

09:29.870 --> 09:31.900
That's what I believe.

09:32.870 --> 09:35.150
Remy's that kind of girl.

09:35.650 --> 09:38.920
When I look at her, I feel at ease.

09:40.050 --> 09:42.290
You love Remy, don't you?

09:44.510 --> 09:48.950
I didn't realize it at the beginning, but after being separated, I did.

09:49.470 --> 09:52.260
I thought I was saving her,

09:52.260 --> 09:55.010
but now I know I wasn't.

09:55.010 --> 09:58.630
The one who was saved was me, more likely...

10:03.110 --> 10:08.010
If Remy were my daughter, how nice it would be.

10:08.630 --> 10:10.880
If Remy was by Arthur's side...

10:11.990 --> 10:15.540
Ah... I'm talking nonsense. Sorry...

10:16.160 --> 10:18.750
Please feel at home and take a rest.

10:28.140 --> 10:29.220
Those birds...

10:29.220 --> 10:31.400
Where are they flying away to?

10:31.400 --> 10:33.210
Maybe to Africa.

10:33.210 --> 10:36.830
Before the winter comes, they fly to Africa.

10:36.830 --> 10:38.230
Hmmmm.

11:00.350 --> 11:02.290
See! Look.

11:02.290 --> 11:03.770
There's another flock.

11:03.770 --> 11:06.610
There is. Wonderful.

11:12.620 --> 11:13.720
Mother.

11:41.040 --> 11:43.040
Mr.Vitalis, good morning.

11:44.080 --> 11:45.650
Good morning, everyone.

11:48.070 --> 11:50.920
May I go to the ranch with Arthur?

11:50.920 --> 11:52.300
He's going to show me the cows.

11:52.930 --> 11:53.840
All right.

11:54.700 --> 11:56.730
I can take them, right?

11:56.730 --> 11:58.470
No... Leave them here.

11:58.470 --> 11:59.350
Huh?

12:04.930 --> 12:06.610
Go and have fun.

12:07.610 --> 12:08.410
Okay.

12:10.760 --> 12:11.600
Remy.

12:12.350 --> 12:12.990
What is it?

12:13.640 --> 12:16.490
Remy, you're a bright girl.

12:16.860 --> 12:17.860
Yes.

12:17.860 --> 12:20.820
That's what I was told by the people in Chavanon village,

12:20.820 --> 12:22.500
bright and cheerful.

12:24.190 --> 12:26.480
Don't lose it.

12:26.480 --> 12:28.000
Cheerfulness is strength

12:28.410 --> 12:29.580
and hope.

12:44.880 --> 12:49.070
Arthur has been waiting for you patiently. Go now.

12:49.390 --> 12:51.730
Okay, I'm going.

13:11.620 --> 13:13.770
This cow looks like Rousette.

13:13.770 --> 13:15.380
Rousette?

13:16.230 --> 13:18.890
The cow we kept when we were living in Chavanon village.

13:20.050 --> 13:23.220
She produced a lot of good milk.

13:23.780 --> 13:28.100
My sister, Nana, and I sang a song to her every morning.

13:28.720 --> 13:31.230
Remy, you loved Chavanon village, didn't you?

13:31.670 --> 13:34.170
Yes, I loved it very much.

13:34.720 --> 13:37.470
There's no village like it.

13:39.270 --> 13:44.400
You must have been sad when you left the village and your mother and sister.

13:45.060 --> 13:46.500
Yes, I was sad.

13:46.870 --> 13:50.770
But it was good that I left the village.

13:54.840 --> 13:55.800
Remy.

13:56.650 --> 13:58.940
But now I'm not sad,

13:59.030 --> 14:03.310
because I'm with Mr. Vitalis and Joli-Coeur and everyone.

14:05.950 --> 14:06.930
Heh?

14:07.390 --> 14:09.270
Are you leaving now?

14:10.050 --> 14:13.770
I want to go to Paris before the real winter comes.

14:18.760 --> 14:20.570
I see.

14:20.570 --> 14:23.250
It won't help if I stop you.

14:23.250 --> 14:24.790
I have a favor to ask of you.

14:24.790 --> 14:25.790
Yes?

14:26.390 --> 14:28.660
Will you let Remy stay here?

14:29.100 --> 14:29.820
Huh?

14:31.080 --> 14:32.720
What did you say?

14:32.720 --> 14:33.740
Let Remy

14:34.390 --> 14:36.170
stay with me?

14:37.400 --> 14:40.380
I lost my horse carriage after the arson incident.

14:40.980 --> 14:44.510
It will take a while to rebuild the troupe.

14:44.840 --> 14:48.090
It will be a hard trip for a little kid.

14:48.090 --> 14:50.320
Will you accept her?

14:52.220 --> 14:56.110
And she also needs a mother.

14:58.020 --> 14:59.110
Mr. Vitalis.

15:02.320 --> 15:04.640
Are you all right with this?

15:04.640 --> 15:06.370
Really all right with this?

15:08.850 --> 15:10.800
Please look after Remy.

15:11.860 --> 15:13.790
Please wait.

15:14.590 --> 15:17.880
Please stay here a little longer.

15:17.880 --> 15:18.710
I can't...

15:18.710 --> 15:22.280
But you're leaving without explaining anything to Remy.

15:22.280 --> 15:24.760
It's better that way.

15:28.310 --> 15:31.060
I promise that I'll look after Remy.

15:31.060 --> 15:32.930
I'll raise her with love.

15:56.810 --> 15:59.880
I should have brought Joli-Coeur here too, after all.

15:59.880 --> 16:01.930
You can come here again tomorrow.

16:01.930 --> 16:04.390
I hope we can come here with Mr. Vitalis tomorrow.

16:35.270 --> 16:36.340
Remy...

16:49.680 --> 16:51.990
I'm home, Mr. Vitalis.

16:56.270 --> 16:58.160
Mr. Vitalis?

16:58.160 --> 16:59.070
Remy.

16:59.500 --> 17:01.070
I need to talk to you.

17:01.780 --> 17:03.110
Okay.

17:10.530 --> 17:13.940
Mr. Vitalis... Without me? What?

17:14.930 --> 17:17.040
It's a lie, a lie.

17:17.470 --> 17:23.400
I promised Mr. Vitalis that I would raise you as a daughter of the Milligan family.

17:23.400 --> 17:27.680
Really, mother?
Can we live with Remy forever?

17:28.980 --> 17:30.600
If Remy wants to do so.

17:35.440 --> 17:37.650
You'll stay here, right. Remy?

17:37.650 --> 17:39.440
You're staying with us, right?

17:40.750 --> 17:41.440
Arthur.

17:42.480 --> 17:46.400
I love you very much and Mrs. Milligan too.

17:47.740 --> 17:49.410
I want to stay here, too.

17:50.720 --> 17:52.910
I don't want to separate from you.

17:53.540 --> 17:57.830
It's Mr. Vitalis' hope that you'll live here.

17:57.830 --> 17:59.420
Please stay here, Remy.

17:59.950 --> 18:01.210
But...

18:01.210 --> 18:05.510
But I have to go. Otherwise, Mr. Vitalis will be all alone.

18:06.140 --> 18:07.150
Arthur,

18:07.800 --> 18:10.130
you have your mother.

18:11.100 --> 18:13.030
But Mr. Vitalis,

18:13.720 --> 18:16.360
Mr. Vitalis only has me.

18:16.360 --> 18:19.240
The Vitalis troupe is my family.

18:21.100 --> 18:25.030
Remy. It's all right, really.

18:26.190 --> 18:27.780
I'm sorry.

18:28.120 --> 18:30.640
No, I don't like it.

18:39.530 --> 18:41.420
Thank you very much.

18:41.980 --> 18:45.420
I... I will never forget you all in my life.

18:45.810 --> 18:46.820
Remy...

18:48.940 --> 18:51.890
Arthur, please be kind to your mother.

18:56.770 --> 18:57.600
Goodbye.

18:58.770 --> 19:00.100
Remy... Remy!

19:00.100 --> 19:01.730
Remy!!

19:25.530 --> 19:28.190
Mother, mother!

19:29.750 --> 19:33.800
Remy forgot something, she told me it's her treasure.

19:34.240 --> 19:35.690
Treasure?

19:35.690 --> 19:37.470
Look, this.

19:38.740 --> 19:40.860
This is my Cameo Broche.

19:41.230 --> 19:43.480
It was a gift from my late father.

19:44.300 --> 19:47.480
Remy has one exactly like it.

19:47.840 --> 19:48.990
Eh?

19:49.750 --> 19:52.780
Remy has the same one?

19:52.780 --> 19:56.910
Uh-huh... She had it when she was found as a baby.

19:57.930 --> 19:59.920
It can't be...

19:59.920 --> 20:02.540
Remy... Remy is my daughter?

20:03.860 --> 20:05.280
It must be.

20:05.820 --> 20:08.300
Somebody, somebody come here.

20:10.220 --> 20:12.880
Mr. Vitalis, Mr. Vitalis.

20:13.610 --> 20:15.480
Please don't go without me.

20:16.950 --> 20:19.780
I want to go with you, Mr. Vitalis.

20:20.350 --> 20:23.270
Mr. Vitalis!

20:37.620 --> 20:40.280
What is it, guys?

20:49.210 --> 20:51.130
Mr. Vitalis!

20:51.130 --> 20:52.460
Remy.

20:58.630 --> 21:00.260
Everyone!

21:10.580 --> 21:12.030
Mr. Vitalis.

21:12.320 --> 21:14.110
Mr. Vitalis!

21:18.080 --> 21:21.740
Please take me with you. Don't go without me.

21:24.740 --> 21:25.970
Remy...

21:32.090 --> 21:33.590
Are you sure?

21:33.590 --> 21:34.630
Remy?

21:37.870 --> 21:46.050
Try to love yourself more

21:47.620 --> 21:56.870
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

21:57.160 --> 22:05.600
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:06.820 --> 22:17.730
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:18.230 --> 22:27.860
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:28.130 --> 22:37.870
From the future that gives us our fate

22:38.050 --> 22:46.780
Try to seek for them more

22:47.680 --> 22:51.380
Give your heart to

22:51.580 --> 23:06.790
That person who is also seeking you

23:21.610 --> 23:23.780
Joli-Coeur, hold on!

23:25.830 --> 23:28.580
Mr. Vitalis, I'm all right.

23:28.580 --> 23:31.710
For Joli-Coeur's sake, let's go over the mountain.

23:33.110 --> 23:36.550
<i>The Snowy Mountain of Sadness</i>

23:33.110 --> 23:36.550
Next time:
